  "statement": "The arcade machine in the break room has no `sorted()` built in, so you have to sort the scores by hand.\n\nGiven a list of integers `nums`, return a **new list** with the same values in ascending order. Implement **bubble sort** yourself: repeatedly walk the list and swap neighbours that are out of order. Do not call `sorted()` or `list.sort()`.",
